    "q-214450": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214450",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[4]_{7}?$\n\n- $-3$\n- $6$\n- $18$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue class $[4]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $4$ modulo $7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{7} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=4+7k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={4+7k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,4-2\\cdot 7,\\,4-7,\\,4,\\,4+7,\\,4+2\\cdot 7,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-10,-3,4,11,18,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $18$ belong to $[4]_{7},$ while $6$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
