    "q-86030": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86030",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following residue classes modulo $5$ contain the integer $-7?$\n\n- $[-2]_{5}$\n- $[3]_{5}$\n- $[7]_{5}$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $-7\\in [a]_{5}$ if \n\n$$\n-7≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-7\\in [-2]_{5}$ because $-7≡-2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-7\\in [3]_{5}$ because $-7≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-7\\notin [7]_{5}$ because $-7≢7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
