    "q-86031": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86031",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Which of the following residue classes modulo $7$ contain the integer $-2?$\n\n- $[1]_{7}$\n- $[5]_{7}$\n- $[-9]_{7}$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $-2\\in [a]_{7}$ if \n\n$$\n-2≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-2\\notin [1]_{7}$ because $-2≢1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $-2\\in [5]_{7}$ because $-2≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-2\\in [-9]_{7}$ because $-2≡-9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86031-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I, II, and III",
              "html": "I, II, and III"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86031-b",
