    "q-86033": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86033",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[16]_{7}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $[a]_{7}=[b]_{7}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[16]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $17$ modulo $7.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[16]_{7} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\cdot 7+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\cdot 0+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & =[2]_{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86033-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[0]_{7}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"165\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mn>7</mn></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86033-b",
