    "q-86035": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86035",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-13]_{5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $[a]_{5}=[b]_{5}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-13]_{5}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-13$ modulo $5.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-13]_{5} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-3)\\cdot 5+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-3)\\cdot 0+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & =[2]_{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
